.TH NIRUPI 1 "2026" "NIRUPI" "NIRU desktop manual"
.SH NAME
nirupi \- helper CLI for the NIRU desktop (dwm, themes, session, apps)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nirupi
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nirupi
front-ends the NIRU desktop: theme switching, the session, web apps, the agent,
maintenance and diagnostics. Most commands also have a keybinding (see
.BR "docs/KEYBINDINGS.md" ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B theme apply|status|diff|list|preview NAME|set NAME|menu
Manage the unified palette. All colours come from one file; switching restyles
the whole desktop live.
.TP
.B theme wallpaper IMAGE|mode noir|wallpaper|palette
Opt-in wallpaper-driven palette (needs ImageMagick).
.TP
.B wallpaper set FILE | next | per-tag on|off|toggle|status
Wallpapers, including instant per-workspace (tag) backgrounds.
.TP
.B agent [profile]
Launch the AI agent (opencode).
.TP
.B menu | keys | lock
Control center, keybinding palette, lock screen.
.TP
.B webapp add|list|remove
Manage Chromium app-mode web apps (Helium-first).
.TP
.B browser status|set|reset | updates [--refresh] | status --once|--json
Default browser, system updates and status-bar output.
.TP
.B repos status|pull (--all | NAME...)
Inspect or fast-forward the Git checkouts under
.IR ~/Git .
Only clean, non-diverged branches are fast-forwarded; the nirupi checkout is
updated through
.BR "nirupi update" .
.TP
.B backup [--list|--verify FILE|--restore FILE [--yes]|--schedule|--unschedule]
Configuration backups with verification, restore and optional scheduling.
.TP
.B gc --dry-run|--yes|--legacy|--system
Prune old NIRUPI versions/snapshots, or use the native package manager,
journal and kernel cleanup with
.BR --system .
.TP
.B tune status|plan|apply|revert
Reversible sysctl tuning (swappiness, cache pressure, dirty ratios, inotify,
BBR when available). Never changes governors or zram behind your back.
.TP
.B snapshot status|create [REASON]|list
Create a system snapshot before updates when timeshift, snapper, ZFS or btrfs
is already configured.
.TP
.B explain [--print]
Collect a redacted system-health context and ask the agent to diagnose it.
.TP
.B mission [NAME] | dwm state|tag N|layout NAME
Run a named workspace/app set, or control the running dwm through its own
keybindings.
.TP
.B update | doctor [--fix|--json|--perf] | rollback --all|--configs RUN|--binaries
Self-update, diagnostics and rollback.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/nirupi/
\(em user configuration (status.conf, session.conf, apps.conf, tokens.env,
wallpapers.conf, ...).
.br
.I ~/.local/lib/nirupi/
\(em deployed runtime bundle and versioned binaries.
.br
.I ~/.local/state/nirupi/
\(em backups, legacy archives and installed.env.
.SH SEE ALSO
.I docs/USAGE.md
and
.I docs/KEYBINDINGS.md
in the source tree, or
.BR https://github.com/nirucon/nirupi .
